            <ArticleTitle>A unique scenario for coronary atherectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>131-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite several attempts, balloon angioplasty of a slightly eccentric stenotic lesion in the proximal right coronary artery failed to result in any increase of luminal diameter. Following disruption and partial removal of a fibrous atherosclerotic cap using directional atherectomy, subsequent balloon angioplasty was highly successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
